  "name": "sodiumoxide",
  "description": "Sodiumoxide provides type-safe Rust bindings for the libsodium cryptographic library, focusing on high-speed, easy-to-use primitives for network communication and data protection. It abstracts the underlying NaCl C implementation into ergonomic Rust interfaces for authenticated encryption, digital signatures, and hashing while leveraging Rust's ownership model to ensure memory safety. The project facilitates secure application development by providing robust implementations of modern algorithms like Ed25519, Curve25519, and XSalsa20-Poly1305.",
